  "published": "1900-01-01T00:00:00Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "First release of LDB v2, rebuilt from scratch: nothing of v1 is carried over, and v1 databases do not open. The database and its engine in one package. Engine: a database is a directory with a write-ahead log per table; snapshot reads lock nothing and never wait; commits across tables are atomic, also across a crash; writers of one table are exclusive or optimistic (Concurrency.Optimistic), conflicting only when what they read changed; full, lazy and no durability with group commit; any number of processes on Windows and Linux, a process dying mid-commit stops nobody; fair writer locks that shed load past MaxWaitingWriters; logs bounded by MaxWalBytes, transactions by MaxTransactionBytes. Database: typed tables with fixed-size rows and a heap for long values; ordered, prefix and hashed indexes; unique and foreign keys with restrict, cascade and set null; defaults and auto-increment; blobs as content-addressed files, collected while others are connected; predicates, a planner with index bitmaps and Explain; aggregates and groups a page at a time or from an index alone; keyset pages after a PageCursor; EnsureTableAsync creates a table with its first rows in one commit; CheckAsync accounts for every page; observers, metrics and traces named Axiom.LDB, HealthAsync, DrainAsync. Limits: macOS and FreeBSD open a database from one process only.",
